# Analytics ids (spec §20/§22).
#
# Committed on purpose. These are PUBLIC identifiers: they ship inside the client
# bundle of a static site and are readable in devtools by anyone, so a repository
# secret would hide them from contributors without hiding them from the world. In
# the repo instead, a fork or a local `npm run build` behaves exactly like CI.
#
# The filename is load bearing: Vite loads `.env.production` for `vite build` and
# `vite preview` (mode=production) but NOT for `npm run dev` (mode=development)
# or `vitest run` (mode=test). That is the whole dev/prod gate — it is why
# `services/analytics.ts` needs no `NODE_ENV` check of its own. Do NOT move these
# into plain `.env`, which loads in every mode and would start pushing local
# development traffic into Google Analytics and Clarity session recordings.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-93JSX24SJT
VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=h5dj6tgz2b
# Yandex Metrica tag number. Numeric on purpose: `services/analytics.ts` passes
# it to `ym(…, 'init', …)` as a Number, which is how the tag indexes counters,
# and it is also what `window['disableYaCounter<ID>']` is named after. Its
# Session Replay (Webvisor) is on and deliberately unmasked — see that module.
VITE_YANDEX_METRICA_ID=98818057
